WEBVTT

1
00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:24.109
Let him burn!

2
00:01:24.209 --> 00:01:25.839
You are going to die!

3
00:01:27.254 --> 00:01:29.394
This is the last one!

4
00:01:30.106 --> 00:01:32.337
We have her!

5
00:01:33.777 --> 00:01:35.827
Let's go, boys!

6
00:01:48.058 --> 00:01:51.246
You will never get her! Never!

7
00:02:01.288 --> 00:02:05.008
I've been hit! Keep going! Go!

8
00:02:05.108 --> 00:02:07.277
Alexsandra!

9
00:03:13.442 --> 00:03:15.344
Jackson!

10
00:03:15.844 --> 00:03:17.580
Jackson.

11
00:03:26.021 --> 00:03:28.239
There he is, Dad.

12
00:03:33.862 --> 00:03:35.931
He's alive.

13
00:03:38.066 --> 00:03:39.852
Get him up.

14
00:03:39.952 --> 00:03:41.837
Get him up!

15
00:03:49.378 --> 00:03:51.147
Where is Alexsandra?

16
00:03:52.247 --> 00:03:54.550
Jackson, where is your wife?

17
00:03:54.650 --> 00:03:56.819
She's been taken.

18
00:03:56.919 --> 00:03:58.787
Kidnapped.

19
00:04:00.289 --> 00:04:02.558
Bring me all the bullets you can.

20
00:04:02.658 --> 00:04:04.794
It'll be light soon.

21
00:04:45.333 --> 00:04:48.410
Brought every rifle bullet
we could find.

22
00:04:48.510 --> 00:04:50.573
Thank you, Timothy.

23
00:04:53.125 --> 00:04:54.515
You know where they headed?

24
00:04:54.615 --> 00:04:57.875
Down the south trail,
towards New Mexico.

25
00:04:58.680 --> 00:05:01.016
They spoke Spanish.

26
00:05:01.116 --> 00:05:05.324
If I'm right, I've got a friend down
that way. He can help me out.

27
00:05:05.654 --> 00:05:08.757
I made this map myself 15 years ago.

28
00:05:08.857 --> 00:05:11.345
Now, there'll be new routes up there,
they'll turn you around.

29
00:05:11.446 --> 00:05:14.097
But you watch the mountains,
and they'll be your guide.

30
00:05:18.366 --> 00:05:20.319
You be careful.

31
00:05:20.419 --> 00:05:22.655
I haven't met your new bride yet.

32
00:05:22.755 --> 00:05:26.584
And I don't know what kinda mess
you got yourself into with these Mexicans,

33
00:05:26.955 --> 00:05:30.347
but you seem like a fine man.
I wish you the best in getting her back.

34
00:08:42.904 --> 00:08:44.873
Yeah.

35
00:08:45.073 --> 00:08:47.276
That's a good boy.

36
00:12:37.172 --> 00:12:39.241
Where is she?

37
00:12:41.770 --> 00:12:44.825
You will get what you deserve.

38
00:12:46.216 --> 00:12:48.076
You will get yours.

39
00:12:53.989 --> 00:12:55.827
Hmm?

40
00:12:56.377 --> 00:12:57.870
Where is she?

41
00:12:59.461 --> 00:13:01.623
She's gone.

42
00:13:02.197 --> 00:13:03.666
And you'll die.

43
00:13:12.432 --> 00:13:16.151
You are the damned.

44
00:14:53.275 --> 00:14:55.344
Hear that, Ace?

45
00:17:59.727 --> 00:18:02.264
How do you like that?

46
00:18:11.954 --> 00:18:12.949
Ah!

47
00:18:17.178 --> 00:18:18.899
What are you doing?

48
00:18:26.921 --> 00:18:29.248
That wasn't very nice!

49
00:19:33.454 --> 00:19:34.636
Excuse me.

50
00:19:37.091 --> 00:19:38.418
Sir!

51
00:19:57.144 --> 00:19:58.871
Sir.

52
00:20:00.515 --> 00:20:03.269
Look, I'm in a hurry.

53
00:20:11.159 --> 00:20:13.428
I'm no thief.

54
00:20:13.799 --> 00:20:15.754
My wife.

55
00:20:16.431 --> 00:20:18.292
She was taken.

56
00:20:20.969 --> 00:20:22.930
Down the south trail.

57
00:20:24.572 --> 00:20:26.633
By Mexicans.

58
00:20:32.013 --> 00:20:34.273
I need to get her back.

59
00:20:38.153 --> 00:20:42.143
I see a rider. Three men, one woman.

60
00:20:42.340 --> 00:20:43.534
Ah-ah-ah!

61
00:20:46.111 --> 00:20:47.571
Money.

62
00:21:00.824 --> 00:21:02.618
Two.

63
00:21:03.678 --> 00:21:05.480
Five.

64
00:21:05.580 --> 00:21:07.590
No wife.

65
00:21:09.583 --> 00:21:11.344
What?

66
00:21:12.653 --> 00:21:16.115
No talk... no wife.

67
00:21:25.867 --> 00:21:28.604
Go now, or I shoot.

68
00:21:28.704 --> 00:21:30.196
Ah!

69
00:21:36.644 --> 00:21:40.139
Well, sometimes,
I just can't help myself.

70
00:21:42.984 --> 00:21:44.777
Huh.

71
00:22:21.788 --> 00:22:24.150
Hello, sir.

72
00:22:24.626 --> 00:22:27.453
Pleased to make your acquaintance.

73
00:22:30.864 --> 00:22:33.377
Just to keep you informed...

74
00:22:33.477 --> 00:22:36.621
this is my road, and as such,

75
00:22:36.721 --> 00:22:40.174
I collect a toll from all travelers
for safe passage.

76
00:22:40.274 --> 00:22:42.135
What kind of toll?

77
00:22:42.710 --> 00:22:45.029
Everything you got.

78
00:22:46.881 --> 00:22:49.366
Maybe even your soul.

79
00:22:53.053 --> 00:22:56.724
- Your horse looks real nice.
- The horse stays.

80
00:22:56.824 --> 00:22:59.328
Well, that is not your decision to make.

81
00:22:59.428 --> 00:23:01.996
You're on my road!

82
00:23:02.196 --> 00:23:04.966
And you will pay my price.

83
00:23:05.066 --> 00:23:09.386
And my price includes that horse.

84
00:23:14.842 --> 00:23:16.471
Are you lookin' to die?

85
00:23:20.415 --> 00:23:22.719
You look like you wanna die.

86
00:23:23.784 --> 00:23:25.887
You like killing unarmed men, don't you?

87
00:23:28.756 --> 00:23:31.292
I just like killin' men.

88
00:23:31.392 --> 00:23:34.829
Especially when their conversation
bores me so.

89
00:23:40.802 --> 00:23:43.054
Do I know you?

90
00:23:47.108 --> 00:23:50.161
You look awful familiar to me.

91
00:23:59.654 --> 00:24:01.456
Yes.

92
00:24:01.956 --> 00:24:05.860
I think I do know you. Yes, I do.

93
00:24:08.195 --> 00:24:11.799
We look tough, we act tough,

94
00:24:11.899 --> 00:24:15.561
but in the end,
we're just lonely, scared men.

95
00:24:19.774 --> 00:24:23.037
Well, I know a soldier when I see one.

96
00:24:24.011 --> 00:24:27.197
You looking for a way to forget the war?

97
00:24:27.682 --> 00:24:30.651
Forget all the horrible,
horrible things you did.

98
00:24:30.751 --> 00:24:32.728
Shut up right now.

99
00:24:33.187 --> 00:24:35.472
Oh, I like that.

100
00:24:37.725 --> 00:24:40.668
You know, I'd like to know
more about you.

101
00:24:41.695 --> 00:24:44.799
How does it make you feel...

102
00:24:44.899 --> 00:24:47.251
when I do that?

103
00:24:50.505 --> 00:24:53.259
Answer me, goddammit!

104
00:24:56.544 --> 00:24:57.965
Open up.

105
00:25:01.148 --> 00:25:03.334
You scared?

106
00:25:03.718 --> 00:25:05.987
Well, don't be scared.

107
00:25:06.087 --> 00:25:09.657
Sometimes I think about
doing it two, three times a day.

108
00:25:10.257 --> 00:25:12.104
Ah!

109
00:25:19.100 --> 00:25:20.652
That's my answer.

110
00:25:22.503 --> 00:25:24.639
I'm gonna kill you for that. Ah!

111
00:25:24.739 --> 00:25:26.041
Ah!

112
00:27:27.862 --> 00:27:30.264
Yeah, easy, boy.

113
00:27:30.364 --> 00:27:32.483
Easy, boy.

114
00:27:57.604 --> 00:27:58.944
Ah!

115
00:28:06.228 --> 00:28:09.079
He's going for his gun!

116
00:28:09.256 --> 00:28:11.762
Let's go! Let's go!

117
00:28:16.796 --> 00:28:20.831
Oh, Ace. Oh, Ace. Ah...

118
00:28:22.249 --> 00:28:24.267
Oh, no...

119
00:28:27.288 --> 00:28:30.711
I'm sorry. I'm so sorry.

120
00:28:36.330 --> 00:28:38.615
I'm so sorry, pal.

121
00:28:40.551 --> 00:28:42.237
Good boy.

122
00:31:49.857 --> 00:31:53.240
Only one thing I enjoy more
than killing a man.

123
00:31:56.497 --> 00:32:00.116
Watching a man die all by himself.

124
00:32:07.874 --> 00:32:10.694
Death might be a favor to you.

125
00:32:27.061 --> 00:32:29.430
How you doing, friend?

126
00:32:29.530 --> 00:32:31.032
You still with us?

127
00:32:37.204 --> 00:32:38.973
What's that?

128
00:32:39.073 --> 00:32:41.109
Fuck you.

129
00:32:42.809 --> 00:32:45.812
Well, I don't know
if I can honor your dying wish,

130
00:32:45.912 --> 00:32:48.856
which really is sad for me.

131
00:32:49.316 --> 00:32:51.609
Just... just kill me.

132
00:32:52.719 --> 00:32:56.590
No, no, no, no, not so fast.

133
00:32:56.690 --> 00:33:01.511
Why, this is the best moment.
Now, we don't want to rush this.

134
00:33:13.439 --> 00:33:17.258
Just leave... leave me alone.

135
00:33:42.369 --> 00:33:44.856
You know what I find most sad about you?

136
00:33:47.073 --> 00:33:50.086
You are all alone...

137
00:33:50.911 --> 00:33:54.698
in a world that don't celebrate
being alone.

138
00:35:14.297 --> 00:35:21.103
Be thankful my son dragged you here
behind his horse.

139
00:35:21.880 --> 00:35:29.966
There are stories of a killer
on the trail.

140
00:36:47.724 --> 00:36:50.378
He awakens. Look at him.

141
00:36:51.028 --> 00:36:54.304
He awakens and does not know
where he is.

142
00:37:00.700 --> 00:37:02.919
Where are my guns?

143
00:37:20.006 --> 00:37:23.332
This one wants to steal a horse.

144
00:37:39.551 --> 00:37:44.437
You brought an evil white man
into our camp.

145
00:37:46.684 --> 00:37:51.188
This diseased filth needs to go.

146
00:37:51.388 --> 00:37:55.287
At the last village
they told a story about

147
00:37:55.387 --> 00:37:59.280
a killer out there killing men
and taking women.

148
00:37:59.380 --> 00:38:02.324
You saw him.

149
00:38:02.424 --> 00:38:04.610
He was possessed by evil spirits!

150
00:38:04.710 --> 00:38:06.970
Seven winters...

151
00:38:07.070 --> 00:38:09.590
Seven women.

152
00:38:10.290 --> 00:38:18.386
Father, it is my duty to honor
my commitment to save his life.

153
00:38:19.566 --> 00:38:21.962
Go on, son.

154
00:38:22.903 --> 00:38:27.609
I tried to force him into cold waters
with my bow.

155
00:38:28.033 --> 00:38:36.289
When his gun overcame me
he spared my life.

156
00:38:48.128 --> 00:38:55.344
Your foolishness has brought
a great burden.

157
00:38:56.186 --> 00:39:03.592
We will find out what kind of man
you have brought amongst us.

158
00:39:08.406 --> 00:39:11.727
Bring him to the sweat lodge.

159
00:39:15.756 --> 00:39:20.291
Let us see how the white man
likes our peyote.

160
00:39:39.159 --> 00:39:42.104
What'd you... what'd you do?

161
00:40:25.939 --> 00:40:29.196
You've got to kill yourself
to end this, Jackson.

162
00:40:29.710 --> 00:40:32.579
You need to end your own life, Jackson.

163
00:40:33.530 --> 00:40:37.117
- No.
- You were supposed to look out for me.

164
00:40:37.217 --> 00:40:39.953
You know, that's what older brothers do.

165
00:40:40.257 --> 00:40:41.921
No.

166
00:40:42.021 --> 00:40:44.207
It's time to die.

167
00:40:48.528 --> 00:40:49.586
No.

168
00:40:51.531 --> 00:40:54.263
Why'd you shoot me, Jackson?

169
00:40:55.535 --> 00:40:58.442
Your own brother, Jackson.

170
00:41:05.228 --> 00:41:07.183
No!

171
00:41:07.547 --> 00:41:11.307
I didn't mean... I didn't mean
to kill... I didn't mean to...

172
00:41:11.407 --> 00:41:13.136
No!

173
00:41:22.457 --> 00:41:27.043
This one must go now.

174
00:41:31.775 --> 00:41:35.220
This man is your responsibility.

175
00:41:35.320 --> 00:41:38.146
You have honored your debt to him.

176
00:41:42.345 --> 00:41:51.270
Give him your horse so he leaves
and never comes back.

177
00:42:47.146 --> 00:42:48.531
Thank you.

178
00:43:24.479 --> 00:43:27.813
May you find your way.

179
00:43:38.514 --> 00:43:39.967
Wait.

180
00:43:59.419 --> 00:44:02.438
No. For... for you.

181
00:44:05.158 --> 00:44:07.445
Hey! Hey! Ah!

182
00:44:07.811 --> 00:44:09.978
Crazy man!

183
00:44:11.643 --> 00:44:13.929
Go now!

184
00:44:17.307 --> 00:44:21.228
Crazy man. Go. Go now!

185
00:44:22.454 --> 00:44:26.635
Crazy man! Go now!

186
00:45:36.349 --> 00:45:37.651
Ah!

187
00:45:38.251 --> 00:45:39.536
Ah!

188
00:47:57.523 --> 00:47:59.608
Mr. Carver?

189
00:48:02.261 --> 00:48:04.180
It's Jackson.

190
00:48:07.833 --> 00:48:10.303
You remember me?

191
00:48:10.403 --> 00:48:14.107
Yes, sir... I know who you are.

192
00:48:14.207 --> 00:48:16.459
Who could forget?

193
00:48:19.079 --> 00:48:21.982
Ah, this is my granddaughter.

194
00:48:22.482 --> 00:48:25.868
This is my acquaintance, Jackson.

195
00:48:27.186 --> 00:48:30.994
- Hello.
- Pleased to meet you.

196
00:48:31.257 --> 00:48:35.762
We served in the war together.
Rebecca lives with me now.

197
00:48:36.062 --> 00:48:37.864
How long's it been, huh?

198
00:48:37.964 --> 00:48:40.649
Hmm. Seven years in May.

199
00:48:43.169 --> 00:48:46.422
Yeah. Yeah, that's about right.

200
00:48:48.407 --> 00:48:50.410
I didn't know you had a family.

201
00:48:52.545 --> 00:48:55.815
You look like you had
a really rough journey.

202
00:48:55.915 --> 00:48:58.300
What brings you to my door?

203
00:48:58.785 --> 00:49:02.020
My wife. She's...

204
00:49:03.089 --> 00:49:05.481
She's been kidnapped.

205
00:49:06.092 --> 00:49:07.994
She's taken.

206
00:49:09.294 --> 00:49:11.147
Taken from me.

207
00:49:11.897 --> 00:49:15.951
Wife? I'm so sorry to hear that.

208
00:49:17.904 --> 00:49:21.607
Anything I can do
to get you back on the trail?

209
00:49:21.707 --> 00:49:24.394
I could use a proper saddle.

210
00:49:24.494 --> 00:49:25.729
My horse.

211
00:49:25.829 --> 00:49:29.583
Certainly. I have a small shed.
It's yours.

212
00:49:30.083 --> 00:49:34.253
Now, whatever you need. Keep the saddle.

213
00:49:34.372 --> 00:49:35.688
Thank you.

214
00:49:35.788 --> 00:49:38.173
I'll meet you over there.

215
00:50:34.580 --> 00:50:36.049
Grandfather, what's wrong?

216
00:50:36.149 --> 00:50:39.352
He's killed more men
than you met in your lifetime.

217
00:50:39.452 --> 00:50:43.557
You load your gun like I showed you,
and if anything happens to me, Rebecca,

218
00:50:43.657 --> 00:50:45.750
you will run from here.

219
00:50:45.850 --> 00:50:48.227
Do you hear me? Do as I tell you.

220
00:50:48.327 --> 00:50:52.214
You will run from this man
and you do not look back.

221
00:50:52.598 --> 00:50:54.404
Run for your life.

222
00:50:55.268 --> 00:50:57.353
Grandpa!

223
00:51:00.673 --> 00:51:04.661
You run... if anything happens to me.

224
00:51:28.034 --> 00:51:30.536
Uh, you have any...

225
00:51:30.636 --> 00:51:32.671
water for my horse?

226
00:51:33.386 --> 00:51:36.158
Pond water's not the best water.

227
00:51:36.742 --> 00:51:39.877
Follow me, son.
Let's walk down to the creek.

228
00:51:40.913 --> 00:51:43.149
So you're headed south, huh?

229
00:51:43.249 --> 00:51:45.968
- Yeah, that's right.
- Hmm.

230
00:51:46.552 --> 00:51:49.221
Saw a group of riders, uh...

231
00:51:49.321 --> 00:51:52.508
passing the big trail yesterday.

232
00:51:53.659 --> 00:51:57.213
You know, three riders
and one woman. Mexican.

233
00:51:59.098 --> 00:52:01.122
What time of day yesterday?

234
00:52:01.401 --> 00:52:03.166
Late.

235
00:52:03.266 --> 00:52:05.917
But the sun was still not down.

236
00:52:07.673 --> 00:52:09.392
Huh.

237
00:52:10.409 --> 00:52:13.512
Those Mexicans you... you saw, they...

238
00:52:13.612 --> 00:52:15.830
they took my wife.

239
00:52:16.482 --> 00:52:18.751
They came in the night
and they took her.

240
00:52:18.851 --> 00:52:22.422
Those are awful things
for any man to have to say.

241
00:52:22.522 --> 00:52:25.124
My concern is that those riders

242
00:52:25.224 --> 00:52:27.655
seemed peaceful enough.

243
00:52:28.494 --> 00:52:32.012
But they had the fear of God
in their... eyes.

244
00:52:32.112 --> 00:52:37.956
Look, I'm... I'm sorry to bring stories
of bloodshed and kidnapping to your door.

245
00:52:38.204 --> 00:52:40.873
Those things had to be said.

246
00:52:40.973 --> 00:52:43.025
Those men...

247
00:52:43.776 --> 00:52:46.858
Those men are the worst of their kind.

248
00:52:47.246 --> 00:52:51.017
Why does it strike me
that the last time I saw you...

249
00:52:51.417 --> 00:52:54.220
after some of the things you did
for General Sherman,

250
00:52:54.320 --> 00:52:56.275
the men...

251
00:52:56.375 --> 00:52:59.006
they called you Diablo?

252
00:53:00.359 --> 00:53:02.939
I asked the men what it meant.

253
00:53:03.629 --> 00:53:07.742
And when they told me...
I learned something about you.

254
00:53:08.334 --> 00:53:12.321
No. No, I was just following orders.

255
00:53:13.005 --> 00:53:16.610
I'm a married man
intent on landing my family.

256
00:53:17.610 --> 00:53:20.980
You were eventually...
Sherman's best killer,

257
00:53:21.080 --> 00:53:25.762
and as I recall, you came
to enjoy life on his trail.

258
00:53:26.652 --> 00:53:28.887
Jackson...

259
00:53:28.987 --> 00:53:32.141
I have a granddaughter in my life here.

260
00:53:33.659 --> 00:53:36.562
I was always kind to you, wasn't I?

261
00:53:36.662 --> 00:53:38.398
Yes.

262
00:53:38.898 --> 00:53:41.550
I don't mince my words.

263
00:53:42.501 --> 00:53:45.004
Why did you come here?

264
00:53:45.104 --> 00:53:47.190
I came to ask for your help.

265
00:53:48.641 --> 00:53:51.930
After all these years,
you're still torturing yourself over...

266
00:53:52.030 --> 00:53:54.047
accidentally shooting your brother?

267
00:53:56.849 --> 00:53:59.201
Go home, son.

268
00:53:59.585 --> 00:54:01.837
Leave those people alone.

269
00:54:05.024 --> 00:54:07.476
Oh, I understand.

270
00:54:07.960 --> 00:54:11.881
I fear you haven't been well
since last I seen you.

271
00:54:14.167 --> 00:54:16.927
Once you fetch the water
from that stream,

272
00:54:17.027 --> 00:54:19.521
we'll get you a proper meal.

273
00:54:20.840 --> 00:54:23.142
Then you have to go.

274
00:54:23.242 --> 00:54:25.127
Alright?

275
00:55:02.548 --> 00:55:06.847
Please! You can have anything you want,
but please don't hurt us.

276
00:55:07.620 --> 00:55:10.022
You gonna look at me like that?

277
00:55:10.122 --> 00:55:13.159
All I needed was a little bit
of fucking help from you.

278
00:55:15.094 --> 00:55:17.346
That's all I needed.

279
00:55:21.801 --> 00:55:24.304
Ah, there he is!

280
00:55:24.404 --> 00:55:26.640
Our intrepid trail traveler.

281
00:55:27.840 --> 00:55:30.526
I just can't seem to lose you.

282
00:55:31.977 --> 00:55:34.446
Well, what can I say?

283
00:55:34.546 --> 00:55:37.717
- I've become attached.
- Jackson...

284
00:55:37.817 --> 00:55:41.504
stop this insanity right now.

285
00:55:41.604 --> 00:55:44.240
Yeah, your fight's with me.

286
00:55:44.590 --> 00:55:47.155
My fight is with everybody.

287
00:55:47.493 --> 00:55:49.863
Lovely granddaughter he has in there.

288
00:55:51.063 --> 00:55:53.366
- No.
- Benjamin, how old is she?

289
00:55:53.766 --> 00:55:56.002
Please, just leave my granddaughter
alone. Please.

290
00:55:56.102 --> 00:55:57.904
Shhh. Shhh-shhh.

291
00:55:58.004 --> 00:56:02.107
Please, Jackson. I mean you no harm.

292
00:56:02.207 --> 00:56:04.176
I can help you.

293
00:56:04.276 --> 00:56:07.447
Yeah, I... I will go with you...

294
00:56:07.547 --> 00:56:10.015
and bring your wife back.

295
00:56:10.365 --> 00:56:12.851
You had your chance.

296
00:56:15.637 --> 00:56:18.190
Now say your prayers.

297
00:56:23.913 --> 00:56:25.190
Say 'em!

298
00:56:32.588 --> 00:56:35.123
For if we live...

299
00:56:35.223 --> 00:56:37.326
we live to the Lord.

300
00:56:37.426 --> 00:56:39.178
Louder.

301
00:56:39.762 --> 00:56:41.997
If we die...

302
00:56:42.097 --> 00:56:43.321
we die to the Lord.

303
00:56:43.421 --> 00:56:47.319
- Louder, goddammit! I want to hear it!
- Whether we live or we die...

304
00:56:47.419 --> 00:56:51.065
we are to the Lord!

305
00:56:51.165 --> 00:56:54.276
Our Father, who art in Heaven...

306
00:56:54.376 --> 00:56:57.610
- Louder!
- Hallowed be thy name!...

307
00:56:57.710 --> 00:57:00.754
- Louder!
- Thy Kingdom come, thy...

308
00:57:00.854 --> 00:57:04.420
- Louder, goddammit!
- Give us this day our daily bread...

309
00:57:04.520 --> 00:57:06.622
You should've never questioned me.

310
00:57:06.722 --> 00:57:11.144
- And forgive us our trespasses as...
- You better hope he's listening.

311
01:00:43.877 --> 01:00:47.356
- Where is César?
- I want to leave.

312
01:00:47.764 --> 01:00:49.441
Over there.

313
01:00:53.762 --> 01:00:56.096
Let's go, César!

314
01:00:56.496 --> 01:01:00.742
Relax, Guillermo,
we are almost to the house!

315
01:01:59.785 --> 01:02:01.527
No!

316
01:02:06.621 --> 01:02:08.440
No.

317
01:02:08.657 --> 01:02:11.064
- Guillermo!
- Stay!

318
01:02:11.164 --> 01:02:13.596
- Guillermo!
- Alexsandra!

319
01:02:13.696 --> 01:02:16.784
- Ah!
- Don't be afraid! Let's go!

320
01:02:17.867 --> 01:02:19.785
Guillermo!

321
01:02:44.526 --> 01:02:46.245
César! No!

322
01:02:49.797 --> 01:02:53.390
No! No! He will kill us all.

323
01:03:00.388 --> 01:03:01.919
Let's go!

324
01:03:02.019 --> 01:03:04.168
We have to get her to safety!

325
01:04:03.393 --> 01:04:05.909
Listen! Listen!

326
01:04:06.009 --> 01:04:08.302
Get the children!

327
01:04:09.174 --> 01:04:11.530
Get into the house!

328
01:04:11.630 --> 01:04:13.338
Fast! Fast! Fast!

329
01:06:38.193 --> 01:06:40.979
Alexsandra!

330
01:07:01.750 --> 01:07:03.835
Where is she?

331
01:07:10.592 --> 01:07:13.044
Bring her to me!

332
01:07:14.696 --> 01:07:17.715
Or I'll kill every last one of you.

333
01:07:24.139 --> 01:07:25.934
Ah!

334
01:07:27.609 --> 01:07:29.120
Ah!

335
01:07:53.615 --> 01:07:55.687
Mama!

336
01:08:05.781 --> 01:08:07.458
Ah!

337
01:08:39.269 --> 01:08:42.395
My sister will never be with you.

338
01:08:54.896 --> 01:08:57.978
That might just be a favor to you.

339
01:09:04.472 --> 01:09:05.891
Take it.

340
01:09:17.953 --> 01:09:20.435
Hmm. Yes, sir.

341
01:09:27.228 --> 01:09:30.749
We don't wanna rush this... do we?

342
01:11:06.161 --> 01:11:08.587
Here he comes! Here he comes!

343
01:11:12.534 --> 01:11:14.519
You go that way.

344
01:12:24.360 --> 01:12:25.638
There he is.

345
01:12:25.738 --> 01:12:27.424
Ah!

346
01:13:56.230 --> 01:13:58.082
Alexsandra.

347
01:14:00.402 --> 01:14:02.287
Alexsandra!

348
01:14:03.171 --> 01:14:05.090
Alexsandra!

349
01:14:06.799 --> 01:14:09.650
Why have you done this?
Guillermo's my husband.

350
01:14:10.250 --> 01:14:12.766
Come out and face me! Come out now!

351
01:14:13.481 --> 01:14:15.750
What you wanted was a fantasy.

352
01:14:15.850 --> 01:14:18.937
How many other women
have you done this to?

353
01:14:21.156 --> 01:14:23.274
Alexsandra!

354
01:14:28.029 --> 01:14:30.882
You left me no choice.

355
01:14:32.900 --> 01:14:36.750
I... I had to have you.

356
01:15:03.253 --> 01:15:06.183
If you touch her I will kill you!

357
01:15:09.637 --> 01:15:11.323
You poor man.

358
01:15:44.106 --> 01:15:46.657
No! No! Alexsandra!

359
01:15:50.835 --> 01:15:53.911
I am going to kill you!
I am going to kill you!

360
01:15:55.416 --> 01:15:57.868
Get out of my house.

361
01:15:58.953 --> 01:16:01.443
Go! Go!

362
01:16:20.208 --> 01:16:23.245
No! No! No, please!

363
01:16:23.345 --> 01:16:26.432
No, don't! No!

364
01:16:26.815 --> 01:16:30.547
Stop! Stop it! No!

365
01:16:33.687 --> 01:16:36.457
Please, he's the father of my children!

366
01:16:36.557 --> 01:16:40.205
- Please don't! Guillermo!
- Alexsandra.

367
01:16:54.147 --> 01:16:57.983
I am not afraid. I am not afraid.

368
01:17:01.922 --> 01:17:03.978
Don't do it.

369
01:17:07.711 --> 01:17:09.944
We can stop.

370
01:17:11.089 --> 01:17:13.937
There does not need
to be any more death.

371
01:17:19.033 --> 01:17:21.697
No! No!
